# Go-to-definition across a program-component (ADR-0246), which is the case
# the method is worth having for: the name a reader does not already know is
# exactly the one that was declared somewhere else.
#
# It rests on two things that are not this method's. The imports come from
# `.components`, this tree's build description, read by the same walk the
# diagnostics use (ADR-0238) -- without them `Answer` resolves to nothing and
# there is no defining-point to report. And the compiler's `file` lines are
# the table its `declfile` field indexes into, so the answer names a path
# this server was never told about and had no way to guess.
#
# The workspace beside this file is the one the imports session uses. %ROOT%
# is this checkout, substituted by the harness; the golden is normalised for
# the same reason and its Content-Lengths are blanked, an absolute path being
# as long as somebody's home directory.
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"processId":null,"rootUri":"file://%ROOT%","capabilities":{"general":{"positionEncodings":["utf-8"]}}}}

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"textDocument/didOpen","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"file://%ROOT%/lsp/sessions/workspace/middle.pas","languageId":"pascal","version":1,"text":"{ The middle of the workspace, and the shape that needs the walk.\n\n  There is no `middle.components` beside this file. The sidecar that names it\n  is `client.components`, one directory entry along, and what the server must\n  take from it is the entries *before* this one -- `base.pas` and nothing\n  else. Opening this file with no resolution at all reports `no interface\n  named 'base' has been exported` and then every name that came from it. }\nmodule Middle;\n\nexport Middle = (Doubled);\n\nimport Base;\n\nfunction Doubled: integer;\n\nend;\n\nfunction Doubled;\nbegin\n  Doubled := Answer * 2\nend;\n\nend.\n"}}}

# `Answer` on line 19 of middle.pas is declared in base.pas, which this
# document does not name and the sidecar one directory along does. The answer
# is a URI for a file the client never opened.
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"textDocument/definition","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"file://%ROOT%/lsp/sessions/workspace/middle.pas"},"position":{"line":19,"character":13}}}

